# EJE Job Card Management System — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never
# be committed. NOTHING in this file is a real credential.
#
# The demonstration needs none of these: with no DATABASE_URL the server runs
# the demonstration store and says so on screen, and `npm test`,
# `npm run build` and the browser suites all pass with no database present.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The connection string Drizzle uses for migrations and for the repositories.
# Development. A name containing "dev" is not decoration: a non-production
# process REFUSES a database whose name does not say it is development, or one
# that is not on a local host. See docs/database.md.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://eje:change-me@localhost:5432/eje_dev

# A SEPARATE database for integration tests. The test suite truncates it
# between cases, so it must never point at development or production data —
# `db:test` refuses to run against a URL whose database name is not clearly a
# test database.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://eje:change-me@localhost:5432/eje_test

# Logs every SQL statement. Development only; noisy.
# DRIZZLE_DEBUG=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which persistence the server uses
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decided in `src/data/backend.ts`, from this environment and from nothing a
# browser can set. Leave it unset: the presence of DATABASE_URL is what means a
# database exists, which is the honest signal.
#
#   demo      — force the demonstration store, even where a database is
#               configured. What a sales laptop wants.
#   postgres  — demand PostgreSQL, so a missing DATABASE_URL fails loudly
#               instead of quietly serving demonstration data to the business.
#
# EJE_PERSISTENCE=postgres

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is nothing to configure for a real deployment: passwords are Argon2id
# hashes in `users.password_hash`, and session tokens are random bytes kept in
# `sessions` as SHA-256 digests. No signing key, no shared secret, nothing to
# rotate — see docs/security.md.
#
# The application must be served over HTTPS in production: the session cookie
# is `__Host-` prefixed, which browsers only store on a secure origin.
# `localhost` counts as one, so development is unaffected.
#
# Overrides the demonstration password, which is otherwise stated on the
# demonstration sign-in screen. It is only ever accepted by the demonstration
# backend and never reaches a database.
# EJE_DEMO_PASSWORD=eje-demo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safety
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lets a NON-production process connect to a database the connection guard
# would otherwise refuse — one that names itself production, or a remote one
# whose name says nothing. Deliberate, per-command, never committed:
#
#   EJE_DATABASE_ALLOW=i-understand npm run dev
#
# Production itself does not need it: NODE_ENV=production is the deployment
# saying so, and the guard steps aside.
# EJE_DATABASE_ALLOW=

# `npm run db:reset` EMPTIES a development database and rebuilds it. It must
# name the database exactly, and it is refused against production and against
# any test database:
#
#   EJE_RESET_CONFIRM=eje_dev npm run db:reset
# EJE_RESET_CONFIRM=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp Business Platform (Cloud API)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set BOTH to send real messages. Set neither and a PostgreSQL deployment
# REFUSES to send rather than pretending: see docs/integrations.md. The
# demonstration (no DATABASE_URL) records messages in its visible outbox.
#
# The token must be a permanent System User token, never a temporary one from
# the dashboard. The templates `eje_job_assigned` and `eje_site_location` must
# be approved on the WhatsApp Business account before anything will send.
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Optional; sensible defaults are used when these are unset.
# WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v21.0
# WHATSAPP_API_BASE_URL=https://graph.facebook.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Document storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where job attachments and issued job cards are kept. PostgreSQL deployments
# write the BYTES here; the database holds only the index row that locates them.
#
# Unset falls back to `.eje-storage` beside the application, which is durable
# but probably not where you want a business's documents. SET THIS to a path on
# a volume that is actually backed up. See docs/integrations.md.
#
# The demonstration (no DATABASE_URL) ignores this and keeps bytes in its
# snapshot, which does not survive a restart.
EJE_STORAGE_DIR=/var/lib/eje/storage
